A. Commit message:
spi: omap2-mcspi: Fix IS_ERR() check for devm_clk_get_optional_enabled()

B. Change summary:
The change modifies the probe function to correctly handle the return value of `devm_clk_get_optional_enabled()` using `IS_ERR()` instead of checking for a NULL pointer. This ensures proper error handling when the clock is not available.

C. Compatibility Risk:
Low

D. Fixed Code:
```diff
diff --git a/drivers/spi/spi-omap2-mcspi.c b/drivers/spi/spi-omap2-mcspi.c
index e2400a067a956..add6247d34819 100644
--- a/drivers/spi/spi-omap2-mcspi.c
+++ b/drivers/spi/spi-omap2-mcspi.c
@@ -1561,10 +1561,10 @@ static int omap2_mcspi_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	}
 
 	mcspi->ref_clk = devm_clk_get_optional_enabled(&pdev->dev, NULL);
-	if (mcspi->ref_clk)
-		mcspi->ref_clk_hz = clk_get_rate(mcspi->ref_clk);
-	else
+	if (IS_ERR(mcspi->ref_clk))
 		mcspi->ref_clk_hz = OMAP2_MCSPI_MAX_FREQ;
+	else
+		mcspi->ref_clk_hz = clk_get_rate(mcspi->ref_clk);
 	ctlr->max_speed_hz = mcspi->ref_clk_hz;
 	ctlr->min_speed_hz = mcspi->ref_clk_hz >> 15;
```